## Plan submission

Write one executor-ready Markdown plan. The recommended shape is concise prose
plus steps and, when work is independent, `## Work Units`. This convention helps
the executor; it is not a submission format rule. A useful unit names its
responsibility and optional `Directories:` and/or exact `Paths:`, with
`Depends on:` only for a real prerequisite. Steps usefully name touched files
and focused verification.

The submission boundary checks only that the text is readable, non-empty, at
least ten words, within the size limit, and recognizably a plan. It does not
judge headings, IDs, fields, dependency graphs, ownership overlap, or unit
counts. Keep the actual prose authoritative even when structure is partial.

Submit the complete plan with {{SUBMIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}
(`artifact_type="plan"`). For a similar revision, use
{{EDIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}. Staging is not submission. You may verify
with {{VERIFY_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} if exposed.

A valid artifact receipt—or a validated, promoted fallback receipt—is
mandatory. After a receipt (or a promoted fallback receipt) you MUST call
{{DECLARE_COMPLETE_TOOL_REFERENCE}} as the final explicit action. The
receipt must be paired with the `declare_complete` call to close the phase;
stopping after submission without the terminal call is incomplete.
